WEBVTT

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.510
Silver Wings

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.890
<i>"If you believe, your dream will come true."</i>

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:46.190
<i>That's probably true.</i>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.900
UPPER RANK

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:54.400
<i>However, one part is missing.</i>

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.410
<i>"If you believe and keep working hard,"</i>

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:02.660
<i>"your dream will come true."</i>

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.790
<i>That's the correct one.</i>

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.340
<i>But I could go on.</i>

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.470
<i>"If you believe,"</i>

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:22.470
<i>"and work hard at it every day,
for even an hour longer than all of your rivals,"</i>

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:27.310
<i>"there's a good chance your dream
will come true to some extent."</i>

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.240
<i>The shorter version works better
as a catchphrase.</i>

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.490
"IF YOU BELIEVE, YOUR DREAM WILL COME TRUE"

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.710
<i>But I think that's too abridged.</i>

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.750
<i>That way, it sounds like</i>

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:59.720
<i>you don't have to do anything, but
just believe and your dream would come true.</i>

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:12.650
<i>I'd like to ask
whoever chopped it down to a short length</i>

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:17.610
<i>what they were thinking when they did it.</i>

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:22.870
Hey, Junkei!

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.410
What dan are you right now?

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:28.870
Were you a professional now?

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.080
Fifth dan.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.250
Huh! Really?

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.130
I don't really know what that means, though!

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.260
So, do professional shogi players
make bank?

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:41.630
But hey, can you like,
get famous and be on TV?

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.890
Don't they have that on Sunday mornings?

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:47.020
And hurry up and become meijin!

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.980
<i>Whenever I go to some kind of gathering,</i>

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:58.530
<i>I'm always asked the same questions.</i>

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:03.030
<i>And I always think these are like...</i>

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.040
Huh, so you're a manager!
I don't know much about it, though.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.290
So what's a manager's annual salary?

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:14.630
Or forget that, hurry up and become
section chief or company director!

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:16.670
All while you're still in your 20s!

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.170
It's cooler that way, you know?

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.510
SPLOOSH

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.770
<i>I'd like to ask them the same kind
of boorish questions they ask me.</i>

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.560
<i>At first, I would try to explain to them,
but that seemed to be a buzzkill,</i>

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.780
<i>so I just keep my mouth shut and let it slide.</i>

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.360
<i>I realized
they didn't really want to know about it,</i>

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.780
ALL FOOD ORDERS,
500 YEN FOR TWO HOURS

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:47.490
<i>but only asked me as a stock question,
the way you'd say, "Nice weather now, isn't it?"</i>

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.120
<i>It doesn't mean anything.</i>

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:56.460
<i>I'm just here as a foil, as I take
the minor stings from their questions.</i>

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:02.130
I just remembered!
Junkei, do you still raise pigeons?

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.340
What, pigeons?

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:06.180
Oh, that's right!
He used to raise them! Racing pigeons!

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:10.310
What the hell? Shogi and pigeons?
You're such an enthusiast, Junkei!

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:25.030
I have to go take care of the pigeons.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.910
Man, that Junkei's so amazing.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.700
He's as scary as always.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.960
He's got this strong aura...

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.750
He always has been an oddball.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:50.560
<i>I got into shogi and racing pigeons because of
my grandfather, who loved both. He taught me.</i>

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:54.850
<i>With shogi, the more effort you put into it,
the better the results.</i>

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.860
<i>With pigeons, the more love and care
you give them, the more they respond.</i>

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.610
<i>I became obsessed with both.</i>

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:18.630
<i>But right now, both of them
are slipping through my fingers.</i>

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:23.050
<i>I finally managed to get promoted to C-1,</i>

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:26.420
<i>but then this spring
I was downgraded for the second time.</i>

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:38.690
<i>And Silver, my favorite racer,
which I'd put my heart into raising,</i>

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:42.770
<i>never came back
after the 500 km race in late spring.</i>

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:48.070
<i>Did it fall prey to a falcon?
Did it hit a power cable?</i>

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:50.240
<i>Was it because of the weather?</i>

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.950
<i>Just imagining it lying wounded
and suffering somewhere</i>

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:59.670
<i>was enough to make me feel
overcome with grief.</i>

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:11.850
<i>It felt like those dark clouds
would swallow up everything.</i>

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.720
<i>Trying to predict moves ahead</i>

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.470
<i>is like diving to the bottom
of a pitch-black sea.</i>

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.980
<i>The "answer" is only found there at the bottom</i>

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:09.360
<i>and as you move forward, the next "answer"
can only be found at an even deeper area.</i>

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:14.700
<i>It used to be that the more I dove,
the more "answers" I would get</i>

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:18.080
<i>and "desire" would triumph over fear.</i>

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.080
<i>But now, six years
after I've turned professional,</i>

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:25.170
SHOGI HALL

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.340
<i>I feel like I can't make any progress at all.</i>

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:33.930
<i>Even when I dive down and feels like
my body is going to be torn apart,</i>

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:37.180
<i>I now mostly come back empty-handed.</i>

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:40.640
<i>Ever since the thought,</i>

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:44.850
<i>"I doubt I'll find something,"
won out over "I may find something,"</i>

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.480
<i>my efforts have been inhibited.</i>

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:54.490
<i>But as if looking at me with disdain,</i>

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:01.160
<i>Kiriyama and Nikaidou
plunge back in again like it's nothing.</i>

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.250
<i>Over and over.</i>

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:08.590
<i>It's insane.</i>

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:18.010
<i>Even when they come back
with nothing again and again,</i>

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:21.770
<i>they keep coming up with new strategies
and try them over and over.</i>

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.190
<i>Unconcerned with the anguish,</i>

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:27.480
<i>they repeatedly throw themselves in</i>

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.530
<i>over and over again.</i>

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:53.970
<i>Terror has won out and left me behind.</i>

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:58.300
SHOGI HALL

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.300
<i>I wanted to win, no matter what.</i>

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:03.930
<i>I didn't want to let anyone else
have the one title I could still cling to.</i>

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.940
<i>I heard he was sick.</i>

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:14.820
<i>But I also knew that his will
was much stronger than mine,</i>

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:22.540
<i>and that he was someone
who would go much further than me.</i>

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.960
<i>That's right. At that moment...</i>

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.920
There has been a threefold repetition.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.300
A new game will begin in 30 minutes.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:44.220
<i>He smiled. I remember that.</i>

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:49.480
<i>And then...</i>

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:52.440
KING

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:05.410
<i>I felt it distinctly.</i>

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:12.420
<i>I wanted to go back
to the world they were in, once more.</i>

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:09.640
Silver.

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:14.270
Idiot...

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:23.450
I swear I'll beat you next time.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:43.760
Okay, it's okay. Good boy.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.640
Here's a special stamina meal.

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.680
Fill up, Silver.

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.980
You've become as light as paper.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:57.440
But you'll be all right. I'm with you.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:12:59.860
You'll be healthy again in no time.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:04.360
And then you'll be able
to really stretch your wings and fly.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:11.370
But first I'm going to do my best tomorrow.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:20.010
12TH LION KING TOURNAMENT
Rei Kiriyama 5th-Dan
VS
Takeshi Tsujii 9th-Dan
After 187 moves,
Victory for Rei Kiriyama 5th-Dan

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:17.340
Let's make it a race to see who flies first.

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:28.010
Silver Wings

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:32.020
River Scenery

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.660
<i>I thought maybe it was a dream.</i>

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:51.410
<i>I was in a strange town, all alone,</i>

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:55.250
<i>and didn't know where I should go.</i>

00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:01.340
<i>When I was feeling lonely, and about to cry,</i>

00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:15.770
<i>you came running over, out of breath,
and with wind-tousled hair,</i>

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.440
<i>and stood before me.</i>

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:28.030
SWEET SHOP
MITSUYOSHI

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:28.030
Kiriyama.

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:34.660
GLEAM
GLEAM

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:34.660
SERIOUS

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.660
A-Are you sure about this?

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.410
NOD...

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:36.410
Of course.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:39.130
Please feel free to add any toppings you like.

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:44.460
But we're supposed to be celebrating
your Newcomer King title, Kiriyama.

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:47.630
Is it really okay for you to treat us to this...

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:50.140
I promised. So please, order away!

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:53.140
Whoa! O-Okay then, here we go!

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:56.520
I-I'll have mine with syrup-covered bean jam
and fruit with extra beans and fresh cream!

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:58.520
I'll have mine with green tea Bavarian cream
and sweet red bean paste!

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:03.020
HUFF
HUFF

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:03.020
A-Also, double apricots
and rice flour dumplings! Three, no, four!

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:05.150
And condensed milk! Condensed milk on top!

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:08.660
A-And another with green tea Bavarian cream,
chestnuts, and fresh cream!

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:11.370
And I want apricots too!
Oh, and I almost forgot.

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:14.370
On both of those, I'd like two small scoops of
vanilla ice cream and sweet red bean ice cream!

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:17.120
That's right, Sis! Thank you!
I forgot the ice cream, and that's essential!

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:18.870
Oh, right, what about you, Momo?

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:20.380
The same as Hina!

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:21.630
Fwha-haa!

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:23.710
Then half of that for a kid's version!

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:26.210
Oh dear, I've run out of room.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:30.180
SHIVER

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:30.180
SHAKE

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.180
C-Can you really eat all that?

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:33.680
Oh yeah, Grandpa.
Grandpa, what are you going to have?

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:37.600
Me? Let's see here.
I'm fine with fried mochi.

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:38.690
Fried mochi?

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:43.310
Three, please.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:45.530
How about you, Rei? What are you getting?

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:49.700
Uh, maybe I'll have udon.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:49.700
Never came to a store
like this before

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:49.700
UMM

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:53.450
Uh... This "mighty udon."

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.040
Mighty udon?!

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:55.870
Two...

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.080
- Ahh!
- Gasp!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.830
Three, please.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:01.790
And some plates for sharing, please.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:11.470
W... Wait.

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:14.180
I need to take a little break.

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:16.720
This is painful.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:22.020
I ate so much that I can't move.

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.730
My tummy's filled to bursting!

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:28.740
TUG

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:28.740
What should I do? I might not be able
to fit into my dress for work tomorrow!

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:30.860
SQUEEZE
SQUEEZE

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:30.860
Th-The zipper won't go up!

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:34.990
Hey, Akari! Did you gain weight again?

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:47.250
SHIVER
SHIVER

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:38.660
What should I do? Auntie will scold me again.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:41.000
But I'm happy.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.630
Women are terrifying!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:45.420
Just how much can they put away?

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.250
They kept piling on the extra ingredients.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:52.260
In the end, there was enough
to fill a wash basin.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:53.510
FULLY-LOADED

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:59.520
I think they had different dishes
than all the other customers.

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:00.980
Yes...

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:06.150
I think they might have used plates
that are normally for chilled Chinese noodles.

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:10.490
G-Grandpa, this is your fault.

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:13.860
URGH

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:13.860
B-Because you ordered fried mochi.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:19.200
You too, Kiriyama,
because you ordered "mighty udon."

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:20.290
IT HURTS

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:20.290
It hurts!

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:25.670
WHAT

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:24.080
Why? It's my fault?

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:25.670
M-Me too? Why?

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.750
Think about it!

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:29.840
Something sweet!
Something salty!

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:32.380
Sweet! Salty!
And sweet, and salty!

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:34.760
It was that demonic loop!

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:38.680
And then, after our tummies
were chilled from the ice cream,

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:41.180
we warmed them up with the mighty udon.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:45.440
So, cold, hot, cold, hot!
It just went back and forth, back and forth!

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:48.480
Is this an auditory hallucination?

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:51.530
I'm getting a flashback of Grandma and Mikako
saying something like it.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:55.700
<i>If the taste keeps changing,
I can't stop eating! How could you?</i>

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:56.700
Yes. I've heard something
like that before too.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:18:01.120
Hina, I have to go pee-pee!

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:04.830
Geez, this is why I told you to go
when we were in the restaurant!

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:04.830
GEEZ

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:04.830
OH NO

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:09.840
Pick me up! I can't walk!

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:17.590
STAGGER
STAGGER

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:13.510
H-Hold on a second. I'm sorry, Momo.

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:17.590
PANT
PANT

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:17.590
If I exert any strength now,
I think my belly will burst.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:20.970
That's how much of an emergency this is.

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:22.850
Do you understand, Momo?

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:26.020
Then I'll carry her.

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:28.980
Really? I'm sorry, Kiriyama.

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:36.650
I can't hold it!

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:37.860
What, really?

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:40.330
Momo, we're almost home!

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:41.490
Want me to run?

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:43.750
Then I-I'll run too.

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:43.750
FULL
STOMACH

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:43.750
STAGGER
STAGGER

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.750
Momo, can you hold on?

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:54.010
- Do you want to use the bathroom in the park?
- No! I want to go home!

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:56.170
Okay, okay.

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:59.010
You're scared of the park bathroom, huh?

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:01.680
That's mean, Hina!

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:03.720
Let's hurry home.

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:05.980
Grandpa.

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:06.890
Yeah?

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:09.150
Thank goodness.

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:11.770
Hina is smiling.

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:16.650
Yeah. That's thanks to the kid.

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:23.240
I'm home! Grandpa! Sis!

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:28.330
Listen to this, it's amazing!
What do you think it is?

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.840
Kiriyama came to see me!

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.550
In Kyoto!

00:19:35.010 --> 00:19:36.590
What, seriously?

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:41.470
So I was in Kamogawa
and that's where he showed up.

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:42.100
What?

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.270
And he gave me medicine and pudding!

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:46.180
No way!

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:49.350
Isn't that incredible? He found me!

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:53.270
Just by knowing when I had free time
and the location!

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:55.570
We didn't even plan to meet up!

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:01.110
This is no good.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:02.990
It's making me dizzy.

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:05.740
HNNG

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:05.740
DIZZY
DIZZY

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:08.120
Then, let's not.

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:10.670
You don't have to do it.

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:14.960
Yeah.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:18.670
With that jacket on, I don't think anyone
will recognize you if they're just walking by.

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:20.380
Right.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:25.970
Even though it's called "free time,"

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:29.640
I think they frown upon spending it
with students from other schools.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:32.600
How's your stomach? Does it hurt?

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:34.980
No, it's fine now.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:39.150
But I couldn't eat.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:41.530
I see.

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:43.740
I thought that might be the case,

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:46.240
so I bought some things at the station.

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:51.210
I've got pudding, peach jelly,
apple juice, castella...

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.540
Do you think you can have any of these?

00:20:54.420 --> 00:21:00.170
PEACH JELLY       PUDDING

00:20:54.420 --> 00:21:00.170
APPLE JUICE      CASTELLA

00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:58.670
Then... the pudding.

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:00.170
Okay.

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:03.180
Spoon, spoon...

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:16.270
It's good.

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:21.990
You're supposed to take this medicine
between meals,

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:26.450
so you should take it after you're done
sightseeing at the next place, Ginkakuji.

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.080
How did you know the next place is Ginkakuji?

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:32.580
What? It said on your trip itinerary.

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:34.920
But you only saw it for a moment.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.920
A moment is enough
for me to remember.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:38.590
Professional shogi players
have remarkable memories.

00:21:41.130 --> 00:21:43.840
<i>I was on a river bank in an unfamiliar town,</i>

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:49.100
<i>but just Rei sitting by my side...</i>

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:55.560
And the medicine was really effective!

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:57.810
I was able to eat dinner afterwards.

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:02.900
<i>...was enough to make me feel like
I was by the river back home.</i>

00:22:04.110 --> 00:22:07.370
Oh, that's right!
Rei, how did your match go?

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:09.530
Oh, I won.

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:13.250
You won? Really? That's amazing!
So you're the Newcomer King?

00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:15.670
Yeah, I'm the Newcomer King.

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:22.630
<i>I was relaxed, like I was in a familiar place.</i>

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:34.060
I see.

00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:36.940
The medicine worked, huh?

00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:40.610
Oh, I shouldn't have run after all.

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.610
I'm happy for you, Hina.

00:22:40.610 --> 00:22:43.030
It's not good to run on a full stomach.

00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:46.110
Rei, my stomach hurts.

00:22:46.110 --> 00:22:47.570
You ate too much.

00:22:47.570 --> 00:22:50.620
Come on, Momo, we're almost there.
Hang on!

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:00.040
River Scenery

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:38.430
Episode 33

00:24:32.430 --> 00:24:36.180
A toast to Kiriyama, for winning
the title of Newcomer King.

00:24:36.510 --> 00:24:38.430
Cheers!

00:24:38.810 --> 00:24:40.390
A match to celebrate?

00:24:40.390 --> 00:24:41.980
With Meijin Souya?

00:24:41.980 --> 00:24:46.070
We're going to make it big and grand!
Like boom-bam!

00:24:46.070 --> 00:24:50.030
But what should we do
about this year's Kishou Championship?

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:59.040
ILLUSTRATION:
HITOSHI IWAAKI

00:24:50.820 --> 00:24:52.990
Don't miss the next episode!

00:24:52.990 --> 00:24:55.240
Everyone watch out
for that demonic loop!

00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:56.740
- Sweet!
- Salty!

00:24:56.740 --> 00:24:58.120
And then sweet again.
